    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d108">

                <pb facs="0225" n="187" sameAs="frus:frus1951v03p1/pg187"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.5/6–2051: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The United States Deputy Representative at the North
                        Atlantic Council</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Spofford</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d108-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-06-20T22:00:00+01:00">June 20, 1951—10
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> Depto 1152. Deputies 48th mtg June 19.</p>
                <p>1. At signature agreement on status NAT forces UK FonMin Morrison said NATO is
                    heart of UK foreign policy. Noted achievements <pb facs="0226" n="188"
                        xml:id="pg188"/> in organizational phase NATO and was confident same
                    cooperative spirit wld prevail in solving major problems of production and
                    sharing burden of financing of defense effort now faced. Expressed hope that
                    NATO, now primarily concerned with defense, wld lead to even closer association
                    within Atlantic community.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d108-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>2. Resolution on interim application military status agreement adopted.<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d108-f3"/> Noted French statement that SHAPE status agreement
                    nearly complete and that similar agreements anticipated for subordinate
                        headquarters.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d108-f4"/>
                </p>
                <p>[Here follows the remainder of the report on the Council Deputies meeting of June
                    19 which was concerned with a variety of other topics.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Spofford</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d108-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d108-f1-content">
                <p>This telegram was repeated to all NATO capitals and to Frankfurt, Heidelberg, and
                    Wiesbaden.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d108-f2" n="2" xml:id="d108-f2-content">
                <p>Regarding the signing of the agreement between the parties of the North Atlantic
                    Treaty regarding the status of armed forces, see the editorial note, <ref
                        target="#pg186">p. 186</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d108-f3" n="3" xml:id="d108-f3-content">
                <p>The resolution, designated D–D (51) 140, was originally approved by the Council
                    Deputies working group on May 31, and the text was transmitted in telegram Depto
                    1028, May 31, from London. It stated that some of the provisions of the
                    status-of-forces agreement could be implemented by administrative action without
                    the necessity for legislation and that such implementation would be useful in
                    the period before the agreement was ratified. (740.5/5–3151)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d108-f4" n="4" xml:id="d108-f4-content">
                <p>Regarding the agreements under reference here, see footnote 8, <ref
                        target="#pg177">p. 177</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
